  "details": "<p><span>An Akkadian inscription of the Suhean ruler</span><span>\u00a0Ninurta-kudurr\u012b-u\u1e63ur was discovered at Dawali.</span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Dawali is a site in the middle of the Euphrates region and was part of the kingdom of Suhu. The city was situated on the east bank of the Euphrates, a few kilometres downstream of Anat (Anatho). The modern city of the same name (Ad Daw\u0101l\u012b) is on the river's west bank. The city's ancient name is not known.",
